Time Complexity:

Let n = size of array

    Building remainder map → O(n)
    Traversing map → O(k)

Overall: O(n)


Space Complexity: O(k)


Approach:

1. Create a HashMap to store frequency of (element % k)
2. Traverse array and fill map with remainder frequencies
3. Handle remainder = 0:
   - Pairs = freq * (freq - 1) / 2
4. If k is even, handle remainder = k/2:
   - Pairs = freq * (freq - 1) / 2
5. For remaining remainders:
   - For each rem, check if (k - rem) exists
   - Add pairs = freq[rem] * freq[k - rem]
6. Avoid double counting of pairs
7. Return total pairs







class Solution {
    public static long countKdivPairs(int arr[], int n, int k) {
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        long pairs=0;
        for(int ele: arr) map.put(ele%k , map.getOrDefault(ele%k,0)+1);
        
        //if map contains 0 (multiple of 4)
        if(map.containsKey(0)){
            long freq = map.get(0);
            pairs+=(freq*(freq-1))/2;
            map.remove(0);
        }
        
        //if K is even and contains k/2
        if(k%2==0){
            if(map.containsKey(k/2)){
                long freq = map.get(k/2);
                pairs+=(freq*(freq-1))/2;
                map.remove(k/2);
            }
        }
        pairs*=2;
        
        //other numbers
        for(int ele: map.keySet()){
            if(map.containsKey(k-ele)){
                pairs+=map.get(ele)*map.get(k-ele);
            }
        }
        return pairs/2;
    }
}
